{"sha":"92b3845cc426dd309a1a0e1b3890156c42e14021","node_id":"C_kwDOJIZg-doAKDkyYjM4NDVjYzQyNmRkMzA5YTFhMGUxYjM4OTAxNTZjNDJlMTQwMjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Janne Lappalainen","email":"34949352+lappalainenj@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-06T04:09:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"Janne Lappalainen","email":"34949352+lappalainenj@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-06T04:09:38Z"},"message":"ci: fix the wheel smoke test in the release workflow\n\nThe build job asserted that `flyvis --help` exits 0. It does not: a bare\ninvocation selects no command, so main() prints the help and returns 1, which\nfailed the job on the first run of the workflow after it landed on main.\n\nCheck what the console script prints instead of its exit status, and grep for a\ncommand that only exists if the registry survived packaging. That is what the\nstep was meant to establish in the first place.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e1d17e5af30e7a458687bb51cf0648562ce952db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TuragaLab/flyvis/git/trees/e1d17e5af30e7a458687bb51cf0648562ce952db"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TuragaLab/flyvis/git/commits/92b3845cc426dd309a1a0e1b3890156c42e14021","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TuragaLab/flyvis/commits/92b3845cc426dd309a1a0e1b3890156c42e14021","html_url":"https://github.com/TuragaLab/flyvis/commit/92b3845cc426dd309a1a0e1b3890156c42e14021","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TuragaLab/flyvis/commits/92b3845cc426dd309a1a0e1b3890156c42e14021/comments","author":{"login":"lappalainenj","id":34949352,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0OTQ5MzUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34949352?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lappalainenj","html_url":"https://github.com/lappalainenj","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lappalainenj/followers